        {
          "id": "step-5-1",
          "claim": "For finitely presented algebraic $\\mathcal F$, a finite presentation computes the sheaf $\\mathcal H om(\\mathcal F,\\mathcal G)$ as a kernel between finite powers of $\\mathcal G$. Exact analytification and [A3] therefore identify its analytification with analytic $\\mathcal H om(\\mathcal F^{an},\\mathcal G^{an})$. Step 4.1 in degree zero identifies morphisms. A finite locally free resolution of $\\mathcal F$ computes global $\\operatorname{Ext}^q$ by the hypercohomology of its Hom complex: locally free Hom is exact, and an injective resolution gives the resulting double-complex comparison. Termwise cohomology comparison and finiteness of the resolution identify algebraic and analytic Ext in every degree. Thus full faithfulness and cohomology/Ext comparison in dimension $r$ are proved before essential surjectivity.",
          "step": "5.1",
          "inputs": [
