        {
          "id": "step-6-1",
          "claim": "A simultaneous bound is available. For $1\\le q\\le r$ take the maximum of the finitely many bounds from step 5.2. If $q>r$, the inductive algebraic dimension bound [F7] makes all relevant cohomology groups of $K_s,Q_s$ in step 4.2 zero at every twist. Multiplication by every nonzero $s$ is then an isomorphism on $H^q(\\mathcal M(n))$ at every integer $n$. The same two-section contradiction starting at any degree forces these groups to be zero at every twist. Thus one integer bounds vanishing for all $q>0$.",
          "step": "6.1",
