          "source": "lem-relative-projective-bundle-k-theory-generators",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]) inherited from the finite\ncoherent-resolution and cohomological suppliers. Let $Y$ be smooth\nquasi-projective over a field and $E$ a rank-$r$ bundle. For\n$q:P=\\mathbb P_{\\mathrm{lines}}(E)\\to Y$, $K^0(P)=G_0(P)$ is generated as a\n$K^0(Y)$-module by $\\mathcal O(a)$, $0\\le a<r$. For $r\\ge1$ and $a\\ge0$,\n$q_!\\mathcal O(a)=\\operatorname{Sym}^a(E^\\vee)$. For $r=0$, the projective\nbundle is empty, its $K$-groups and all $q_!\\mathcal O(a)$ are zero, and the\nassertion of generation is vacuous. This statement has the\ncorresponding dual form for quotient projective bundles.",
