          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC and DC. On a regular Noetherian surface a coherent reflexive module is locally free. For a finite module $M$ over a normal Noetherian domain, a generic vector belonging to $M^{**}$ at every height-one localization belongs to $M^{**}$. For a coherent generic-rank-$r$ module on a regular surface, $(\\wedge^rM)^{**}$ is the determinant line of $M^{**}$.",
