      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Near a point of $L_\\infty$, let $R$ be the regular local surface ring, $t$ a local equation of $L_\\infty$, and $M$ the torsion-free stalk of $\\mathcal E$. Multiplication by $t$ is injective on $M$. Lift a basis of $M/tM\\cong(R/(t))^N$ to obtain a surjection $R^N\\twoheadrightarrow M$ by Nakayama [F8]. If $K$ is its kernel, tensoring with $R/(t)$ is exact on the left because $t$ is injective on $M$; the lifted basis makes $(R/(t))^N\\to M/tM$ an isomorphism, so $K/tK=0$. Nakayama [F8] gives $K=0$, proving local freeness of rank $N$ near the framed line.",
