          "claim": "The Hilbert polynomial gives $\\chi(\\mathcal E(-1))=\\chi(\\mathcal E(-2))=-k$. With the vanishings of step 3.1, $h^1(\\mathcal E(-1))=h^1(\\mathcal E(-2))=k$. The Euler sequence is locally split, so tensoring it by $\\mathcal E$ remains exact; its first map therefore injects $H^0(\\mathcal E\\otimes\\Omega^1)$ into $H^0(\\mathcal E(-1))^3$, which is zero by step 3.1.",
