          "id": "proof-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Direct multiplication gives $\\beta\\alpha=(-z_0B_2+z_2)(z_0B_1-z_1)+(z_0B_1-z_1)(z_0B_2-z_2)+z_0^2IJ=z_0^2([B_1,B_2]+IJ)=0$. The $z_0z_1$ and $z_0z_2$ cross terms cancel pairwise, and the $z_1z_2$ terms cancel. On $L_\\infty$, $\\alpha=(-z_1,-z_2,0)^T$ is injective at every point because $z_1,z_2$ are not simultaneously zero. Thus $\\alpha$ has full rank generically; its sheaf kernel is a torsion subsheaf of the locally free source, and hence is zero.",
