          "claim": "At a point of $L_\\infty$, $\\beta=(z_2,-z_1,0)$ is onto. At an affine point $[1:u_1:u_2]$, failure of surjectivity would give a nonzero $\\lambda\\in V^*$ with $\\lambda B_1=u_1\\lambda$, $\\lambda B_2=u_2\\lambda$, and $\\lambda I=0$. Then $\\lambda$ annihilates every vector $B_{i_1}\\cdots B_{i_m}I(w)$, contradicting stability. Hence $\\beta$ is everywhere onto, so $K=\\ker\\beta$ is a vector bundle of rank $k+N$.",
