          "claim": "Since $(\\overline{\\alpha_i})^\\dagger=\\overline{\\alpha_i^\\dagger}$, the commutator part of $\\mu_{\\mathbb R}$ is $\\overline C$. Also $II^\\dagger=\\overline X$ and $J^\\dagger J=\\overline Y$. Thus $\\mu_{\\mathbb R}=\\overline C+\\overline X-\\overline Y$. Conjugating the source real equation gives $\\overline C-\\overline X+\\overline Y=0$, so the raw expression on such a source solution is $2(\\overline X-\\overline Y)=2\\overline C$.",
