          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "By [A1] and [F3], $\\eta$ is exact, so choose a smooth real one-form $\\alpha$ with $\\eta=d\\alpha$. The ASD equation gives $\\int_{S^4}\\eta\\wedge *_g\\eta=-\\int_{S^4}d\\alpha\\wedge\\eta=-\\int_{S^4}d(\\alpha\\wedge\\eta)=0$, since $d\\eta=0$ and $S^4$ is compact without boundary. The integrand $\\eta\\wedge *_g\\eta$ is the nonnegative squared norm density of the real form $\\eta$; zero integral forces $\\eta=0$ pointwise. Hence $F_{\\det A}=0$ and the determinant connection is flat.",
