        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "The bundle e*E has a canonical flat partial connection δ along D: in a holomorphic frame pulled back from E, differentiate coefficient functions along the fibers of e. Changes of that frame have zero D derivative, so δ is well-defined and flat. Transfer δ to p*H by evaluation. For a local holomorphic section s of H, δ(p*s) is a section of D*⊗p*H. Push down using Ω¹_U≅p_*D* from step 2.1 to define ∇s. The partial Leibniz rule becomes ∇(fs)=df⊗s+f∇s, so ∇ is a holomorphic full connection. Its pullback restriction to D is δ, first on pulled-back sections and then on all sections by Leibniz. It is unique: the difference of two such connections is an End(H)-valued one-form restricting to zero on D at every λ, hence zero by the same cotangent isomorphism. The curvature restricts on D to δ²=0. Connections on overlapping graph charts agree by uniqueness.",
