          "claim": "The section metric is the form induced by b_z(s(z),t(σz)) in [F1]. It is independent of z on each line because that scalar is holomorphic on P¹, and is smooth by the evaluation frames of [F3]. The preceding construction commutes with duals, conjugate pullback and bundle morphisms: each commutes with the canonical relative e-connection and the cotangent isomorphism, and uniqueness in step 3.1 then forces the full connections to commute. Apply this to the holomorphic reality isomorphism E→σ*bar_E*. On the real line locus, the induced conjugate involution fixes the parameter and its real tangent vectors. Thus the induced map H→bar_H* intertwines ∇ with the conjugate dual connection, which is precisely X h(s,t)=h(∇_X s,t)+h(s,∇_X t) for real X. Positivity from [F1] makes ∇ unitary. Arbitrary independent positive forms would not satisfy this identity and are not used.",
