          "claim": "In the Grothendieck group, exactness of the monad gives $[\\mathcal E]=(2k+N)[\\mathcal O]-k[\\mathcal O(-1)]-k[\\mathcal O(1)]$. By [F1], its Chern character is $(2k+N)-ke^{-H}-ke^H=N-kH^2$, because the constant terms cancel to $N$, the linear terms cancel, the quadratic contribution is $-kH^2$, and terms of degree at least four vanish on $Z$. Therefore $c_1(\\mathcal E)=0$ and $c_2(\\mathcal E)=-\\operatorname{ch}_2(\\mathcal E)=kH^2$.",
