    "lem-qftx-asd-penrose-kernel-vanishing": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-qftx-framed-penrose-ward-correspondence-on-s4",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC and the exact projective GAGA comparison used below; its substantial local analytic prerequisites remain unresolved in its own carrier. The local smooth integrable-Dolbeault frame theorem is supplied by the explicit local proof, rather than assumed as a new analytic input.\n\nFor $N\\geq2$, let $\\mathcal M^{\\mathrm{ASD}}_{k,N}$ be the framed unitary ASD sector on the round oriented $S^4$ defined above. On the Ward side take a holomorphic rank-$N$ bundle $\\mathcal E$ on $Z$, a positive Hermitian Ward reality datum, and a unitary framing on $L_\\infty$. Require $\\mathcal E|_{L_x}\\cong\\mathcal O_{L_x}^{\\oplus N}$ for every real twistor line, and require $c_2(\\mathcal E)=kH^2$, where $H=c_1(\\mathcal O_Z(1))$. Then $\\widehat E_x=H^0(L_x,\\mathcal E|_{L_x})$ forms a smooth rank-$N$ Hermitian bundle on $S^4$. For each section of $\\widehat E_x$, extend it holomorphically and uniquely to the first infinitesimal neighbourhood of $L_x$ and differentiate this extension in the family of lines; this defines the Ward connection $\\widehat\\nabla$. The form induced by the positive holomorphic reality pairing is smooth and is preserved by $\\widehat\\nabla$; this is a conclusion, not an independent metric-compatibility assumption.\n\nUnder these hypotheses, the Ward construction gives a bijection between based unitary gauge classes in $\\mathcal M^{\\mathrm{ASD}}_{k,N}$ and isomorphism classes of the specified framed Ward bundles. The reconstructed Ward connection satisfies $F^+=0$ and $q_N=-k$. The inverse sends a framed ASD connection to the holomorphic structure on $\\pi^*E$ whose vertical part is the standard Dolbeault operator and whose horizontal $(0,1)$ part is the connection on the planes $\\ell\\otimes S_x^-$. Both maps preserve the framing, Hermitian form, charge, and compact torus action. Reducible bundles and flat summands are included; no irreducibility assumption is imposed.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
