          "quote": "Assume full AC and DC. Let $Z=\\mathbb C\\mathbb P^3$, let $G=\\operatorname{Gr}(2,4)$ be the complex Grassmannian of projective lines in $Z$, and let $p:\\mathscr L\\to G$ be the universal line family with evaluation map $e:\\mathscr L\\to Z$. Let $\\mathcal E\\to Z$ be a holomorphic rank-$N$ bundle, $N\\geq2$, with a positive Hermitian real structure and a unitary framing on the twistor line at $\\infty$. Assume its restriction to every real twistor line $L_x$ is holomorphically and unitarily trivial. The degree-zero base-change maps at every real line are isomorphisms. Then $(p_*e^*\\mathcal E)|_{S^4}$ is a smooth Hermitian rank-$N$ vector bundle, its fibre at $x$ is $H^0(L_x,\\mathcal E|_{L_x})$, and the evaluation morphism identifies its pullback to the real incidence family with $e^*\\mathcal E$. More precisely, for every real line, there is a complex-open neighbourhood in $G$ on whose entire universal-line family the evaluation morphism is an isomorphism. The framing on $L_\\infty$ induces a unitary framing of this bundle at $\\infty$.",
