          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $S^4$ have the unit round metric and the positive stereographic orientation for $z_1=x_0+ix_1$, $z_2=x_2+ix_3$. Let $E\\to S^4$ be any smooth finite-rank Hermitian bundle with a smooth unitary anti-self-dual connection $A$. On $Z=\\mathbb CP^3$ use the incidence equations $\\mu_1=z_1\\lambda_1-\\bar z_2\\lambda_2$, $\\mu_2=z_2\\lambda_1+\\bar z_1\\lambda_2$, with infinity fibre $\\lambda_1=\\lambda_2=0$. Suppose $F$ is a holomorphic bundle smoothly identified with $\\pi^*E$ and its Dolbeault operator is the ordinary vertical derivative and the $A$-horizontal alpha-plane operator. Then\n\n$$H^1(Z,F\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(-2))=H^1(Z,F^\\vee\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(-2))=0.$$\n\nThis applies to arbitrary reducible and flat summands. It assumes no algebraic-to-analytic GAGA, monad, or inverse ADHM normal form as an independent premise.",
