          "source": "thm-first-hypercohomology-spectral-sequence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For an additive left-exact functor $F$ and a bounded-below complex $K$ with supplied Cartan–Eilenberg resolution $I$, there is a spectral sequence\n$$E_1^{p,q}=R^qF(K^p)\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\mathbb R_I^{p+q}F(K),\\qquad d_r:(p,q)\\mapsto(p+r,q-r+1).$$\nHere $q\\ge0$ and $p\\ge b$ if $K^p=0$ for $p<b$. It is first quadrant after translating $p$ by $b$ and converges strongly with a finite filtration on every target degree. Derived objects use the supplied columns; under DC, or supplied Cartan–Eilenberg comparison and homotopy data, it is natural in $K$ and independent of the resolution from $E_1$ onward.",
