          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-rr-for-projective-space-projections",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]) inherited from the finite\ncoherent-resolution and cohomological suppliers. Let $k$ be an algebraically\nclosed field, let $Y$ be a nonsingular equidimensional quasi-projective\n$k$-scheme of finite type ([[def-smooth-morphism-schemes]],\n[[cor-smooth-variety-classical-scheme-conventions-agree]]), let $n\\ge0$ and let\n$$p:\\mathbb P^n_k\\times_kY\\longrightarrow Y$$\nbe the projection. For every\n$\\alpha\\in K_0(\\mathbb P^n\\times_kY)$\n([[def-grothendieck-group-of-coherent-sheaves-and-vector-bundles-on-a-scheme]]):\n$$\\operatorname{ch}\\bigl(p_!(\\alpha)\\bigr)\\cdot\\operatorname{td}(T_Y)\\;=\\;p_*\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ch}(\\alpha)\\cdot\\operatorname{td}(T_{\\mathbb P^n\\times_kY})\\Bigr)\\qquad\\text{in }A^*(Y)_{\\mathbb Q},$$\nwhere $\\operatorname{ch},\\operatorname{td}$ are the Chern character and Todd\nclass of [[def-chern-character-and-todd-class]], $p_!$ is the K-theory\npushforward ([[def-pushforward-in-algebraic-k-theory]],\n[[lem-k-zero-vector-bundles-versus-coherent-sheaves]]) and $p_*$ is the proper\npushforward on Chow groups\n([[lem-proper-pushforward-of-cycles-well-defined]]). Equivalently, writing\n$\\tau_X(\\alpha)=\\operatorname{ch}(\\alpha)\\operatorname{td}(T_X)$, the diagram\n$$\\begin{array}{ccc}K_0(\\mathbb P^n\\times_kY) & \\xrightarrow{\\ \\tau\\ } & A^*(\\mathbb P^n\\times_kY)_{\\mathbb Q}\\\\ \\downarrow p_! & & \\downarrow p_*\\\\ K_0(Y) & \\xrightarrow{\\ \\tau\\ } & A^*(Y)_{\\mathbb Q}\\end{array}$$\ncommutes. The case $Y=\\operatorname{Spec}k$ is Hirzebruch-Riemann-Roch for\n$\\mathbb P^n$, and the case of a general projective-bundle projection is obtained\nby the same argument applied to the projective bundle formula.",
