          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The Ward construction gives exactly the smooth pullback bundle and vertical/horizontal Dolbeault operator required in [A1], for the same sphere and incidence in [F1]. Thus its two cohomology vanishings apply directly. The dual is again unitary and ASD, since its curvature is $-F_A^t$ and Hodge star commutes with transpose, and its holomorphic operator is the induced dual one. Hence both $H^1(Z,\\mathcal E(-2))$ and $H^1(Z,\\mathcal E^\\vee(-2))$ vanish. This uses the supplier's exact stated conclusion, not an unexposed injective-map premise.",
