          "claim": "Apply [F4] to the diagonal Koszul resolution [F3], tensoring the second factor by $\\mathcal E(-2)$, pushing to the first factor, and twisting that output factor by $\\mathcal O(2)$. Its first page is $E_1^{p,q}=H^q(Z,\\mathcal E(-2)\\otimes\\Omega_Z^{-p}(-p))\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(p+2)$ for $p=-3,-2,-1,0$. Steps 1.2, 2.1 and 2.2 and Serre duality make every term in rows $q=0,1,3$ vanish except possibly $H^1(\\mathcal E\\otimes\\Omega_Z^2)$ at $(-2,1)$. No differential can enter this term; its only possible outgoing $d_2$ lands in $H^0(\\mathcal E(-2))=0$. It therefore survives to $E_\\infty$, but the diagonal construction resolves $\\mathcal E(-2)$ before the output twist and $\\mathcal E$ after that twist; it is concentrated in degree zero and has no degree $-1$ hypercohomology. Since $(-2)+1=-1$, the term is zero. Thus the remaining spectral-sequence row is $q=2$.",
