        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-qftx-linear-twistor-monad-charge-normalization",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\pi:Z=\\mathbb CP^3\\to S^4$ be the oriented twistor fibration with the conventions stated in the following references section, let $H=c_1(\\mathcal O_Z(1))$, and let $E\\to S^4$ be a framed unitary ASD rank-$N$ bundle whose Ward bundle is $\\mathcal E=\\pi^*E$ as a smooth bundle. Suppose $\\mathcal E$ is the cohomology of a linear monad\n\n$$\\mathcal O_Z(-1)^{\\oplus k}\\longrightarrow\\mathcal O_Z^{\\oplus(2k+N)}\\longrightarrow\\mathcal O_Z(1)^{\\oplus k}.$$\n\nThen $\\operatorname{ch}(\\mathcal E)=N-kH^2$, $c_1(\\mathcal E)=0$, and $c_2(\\mathcal E)=kH^2$. For the twistor orientation specified in the Definition, if $u\\in H^4(S^4;\\mathbb Z)$ satisfies $\\langle u,[S^4]\\rangle=1$, then $\\pi^*u=H^2$. Consequently\n\n$$k=\\langle c_2(E),[S^4]\\rangle=-q_N(E,A).$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
