          "claim": "The entrywise-conjugation counterexample remains valid for the literal source equations; it is not a defect in the raw block supplied by [F5]. The source's displayed M also ends its first block row with P* despite declaring P of size k×N, so that entry has N rows rather than k in general. These displays cannot be substituted for an intrinsic real normal-form proof. Retain exactly [A1]'s existence and uniqueness obligation.",
