          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $X$ be a nonempty, connected, compact, oriented, finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable smooth four-manifold without boundary, with Riemannian metric $g_X$. Let $G\\subseteq U(V,h)$ be a compact non-Abelian matrix Lie group in its specified global form, let $P\\to X$ be a smooth right principal $G$-bundle, and let $\\omega$ be a supplied smooth principal connection. Let $B$ be a positive-definite, symmetric, $\\operatorname{Ad}(G)$-invariant bilinear form on $\\mathfrak g$. For any local section $s_i$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=dA_i+\\tfrac12[A_i\\wedge A_i]$. Invariance of $B$ makes the local four-forms $\\beta_B|_{U_i}=\\frac{1}{8\\pi^2}B(F_i\\wedge F_i)$ and $\\gamma_B|_{U_i}=B(F_i\\wedge *_{g_X}F_i)$ restrictions of global forms. Define $q_B=\\int_X\\beta_B$. For a real scalar $g>0$, define the Euclidean Yang–Mills functional by\n\n$$\nS_B(P,\\omega):=\\frac{1}{g^2}\\int_X\\gamma_B,\n$$\n\nwhere the Hodge operator is characterized by $\\alpha\\wedge *_{g_X}\\beta=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle_{g_X}\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_{g_X}$ and acts componentwise on $\\mathfrak g$-valued forms. Then\n\n$$\nS_B(P,\\omega)\\geq \\frac{8\\pi^2}{g^2}\\,|q_B(P,\\omega)|.\n$$\n\nEquality holds exactly in these cases: if $q_B>0$, then $F_i=*_{g_X}F_i$; if $q_B<0$, then $F_i=-*_{g_X}F_i$; if $q_B=0$, then $F_i=0$. Every self-dual or anti-self-dual supplied connection satisfies the source-free Euclidean Yang–Mills equation $D_{A_i}(*_{g_X}F_i)=0$, where $D_{A_i}\\eta=d\\eta+[A_i\\wedge\\eta]$. The statement asserts neither existence nor uniqueness of a connection in any charge sector.",
