          "claim": "When $k=0$, $V=0$. There is exactly one quadruple of maps, all with zero-dimensional domain or codomain. Both moment equations are the unique equality of endomorphisms of $0$; the span of the empty family is $0=V$, and no nonzero subspace of $V$ exists. Thus this datum is stable and costable, and the quotient by $U(0)$ is one point.",
