          "claim": "For the framed ASD connection, $q_B=q_N=0$ by [F2], so the ASD action bound gives $F_A=0$. For two piecewise smooth paths from $\\infty$ to $x$, their concatenation is a loop and is null-homotopic by [F3]. Pull back a cover by coordinate balls with local parallel frames to the compact homotopy square; a Lebesgue number gives a finite subdivision with each cell mapped into one such ball. Transport along a continuous edge is defined using that ball's parallel frame; on overlaps the change between parallel frames is constant, so the definition is independent of the chosen ball. Each cell has identity boundary transport, and multiplying over the subdivision cancels all interior edges. Therefore the loop holonomy is identity and transport from $\\infty$ is path-independent. The resulting sections of a framed orthonormal basis are smooth and parallel in local parallel frames, so the bundle with connection is framed-isomorphic to the trivial bundle with its flat connection. The framing fixes that isomorphism at $\\infty$. Any covariantly constant unitary automorphism preserving the framing is identity, since its value at every point is its parallel transport from the identity at $\\infty$. Thus the framed flat gauge class is unique and has no residual based stabilizer.",
