      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "For $V=W=\\mathbb C$, both commutators vanish. Thus $\\mu_{\\mathbb C}=IJ=0$ and $\\mu_{\\mathbb R}=|I|^2-|J|^2=\\zeta$. Since $I\\ne0$, the words of length zero applied to $I(W)$ span $V$, so the datum is stable. Since $J=0$, the nonzero subspace $V$ is invariant and contained in $\\ker J$, so the datum is not costable; in particular it is not a zero-FI regular datum. By [F2], its positive-FI complex orbit has a representative with $I=1$ after the $GL(1,\\mathbb C)$ change of basis $g=\\zeta^{-1/2}$.",
