      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Matrix multiplication gives $b_z^\\dagger a_z=(-B_2+z_2)(B_1-z_1)+(B_1-z_1)(B_2-z_2)+IJ=\\mu_{\\mathbb C}$. Taking adjoints gives the other off-diagonal entry of $DD^\\dagger$. Subtracting $a_z^\\dagger a_z$ from $b_z^\\dagger b_z$ cancels every scalar and linear-in-$z$ term and leaves $[B_1,B_1^\\dagger]+[B_2,B_2^\\dagger]+II^\\dagger-J^\\dagger J=\\mu_{\\mathbb R}$. This proves both identities with their exact signs.",
