          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "Failure of surjectivity of $b_z^\\dagger=(-B_2+z_2,B_1-z_1,I)$ gives a nonzero covector $\\ell$ with $\\ell B_i=z_i\\ell$ and $\\ell I=0$, contradicting the stable spanning set. Conversely, if the stable word span $S$ is proper, the induced pair on $V/S$ commutes since $[B_1,B_2]=-IJ$ has image in $S$. Its dual has a common eigenvector by [F4], and the resulting covector annihilates $I$ and both rows at the corresponding $z$, so surjectivity fails there. A kernel vector of $a_z$ is a common eigenvector of $B_i$ in $\\ker J$ and contradicts costability. Conversely, on any nonzero common invariant $S\\subset\\ker J$, the pair commutes by the complex equation and has a common eigenvector by [F4], producing such a kernel. This proves both equivalences.",
