        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "step": "4.1",
          "claim": "Differentiate $DP=0$ and its adjoint to obtain $dP\\,P=-D^\\dagger(DD^\\dagger)^{-1}dD\\,P$ and $P\\,dP=-P\\,dD^\\dagger(DD^\\dagger)^{-1}D$. Thus [F3] gives $F=P\\,dP\\wedge dP\\,P=P\\,dD^\\dagger\\operatorname{diag}(f^{-1},f^{-1})\\wedge dD\\,P$. Its nonzero differential blocks are $dD=\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}dz_2&-dz_1\\\\-d\\bar z_1&-d\\bar z_2\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)$. The resulting two-form blocks are multiples of $dz_1\\wedge d\\bar z_1-dz_2\\wedge d\\bar z_2$, $2dz_1\\wedge d\\bar z_2$ and $2dz_2\\wedge d\\bar z_1$, with coefficient $f^{-1}$; the $W$ blocks vanish. Expanding in real coordinates shows that these forms are complex linear combinations of $dx^0\\wedge dx^1-dx^2\\wedge dx^3$, $dx^0\\wedge dx^2+dx^1\\wedge dx^3$ and $dx^0\\wedge dx^3-dx^1\\wedge dx^2$. Each has Hodge star minus itself for the positive Euclidean orientation. Multiplication by the degree-zero matrices $P$ preserves this property, so $F^+=0$.",
