          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "First solve one equation with all other coordinates regarded as parameters $p$. Write $z_j=\\rho w$ on a disk slightly larger than $|w|\\le2$, choose a fixed smooth cutoff $\\chi$ supported in $|w|<2$ and equal to one for $|w|\\le1$, and put $a_\\rho(w,p)=\\rho A_j(\\rho w,p)$. For fixed $0<\\alpha<1$, its $C^\\alpha_w$ norm is bounded uniformly on a compact parameter polydisc by $C\\rho(M_0+\\rho M_1)$, where $M_0,M_1$ bound $A_j$ and its first derivatives. Multiplication is bounded in the matrix Hölder norm by the product rule for increments, and [F1] bounds $K(p)u=T(\\chi a_\\rho u)$ on $C^\\alpha(\\overline D_2)$. Choose one positive $\\rho$ making $\\|K(p)\\|<1/4$ for every parameter. By [F3], $g=1-K(p)g$ has a unique fixed point; $\\|g-1\\|\\le\\|K\\|/(1-\\|K\\|)<1/3$, so $g$ is invertible everywhere. On $|w|<1$, [F1] gives $\\partial_{\\bar w}g=-a_\\rho g$.",
