          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "Gauge by this $g$ on the smaller disk. The transformed coefficient is $A_i'=g^{-1}(\\partial_{\\bar z_i}g+A_i g)$, and $A_j'=0$. The square-zero condition in a smooth frame is $\\partial_{\\bar z_i}A_j-\\partial_{\\bar z_j}A_i+[A_i,A_j]=0$, and it is preserved by the gauge transformation by direct conjugation of $(D'')^2$. Therefore every remaining $A_i'$ is holomorphic in $z_j$. Kill the next coordinate by steps 1.1–2.1 with a cutoff only in that coordinate. Their holomorphic-parameter assertion preserves $A_j'=0$. Continue through the finitely many coordinates, shrinking the respective coordinate disks as needed. The product of the resulting smooth invertible gauges has all transformed coefficients zero, proving the required local frame.",
