        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "thm-qftx-zero-fi-regular-adhm-asd-correspondence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $N\\geq2$, $k\\geq0$, and let $\\mathcal M^{\\mathrm{ADHM,reg}}_{k,N}$ be the quotient by $U(k)$ of the raw data satisfying both zero moment equations and stable-and-costable regularity in the conventions stated in the following references section. Let $\\mathcal M^{\\mathrm{ASD}}_{k,N}$ be the framed unitary ASD sector on the round oriented $S^4$ with $q_N=-k$ in those same conventions. Conditional on the real monad normalization and Ward inputs stated below, the construction gives a $T=(S^1)^2\\times(S^1)^N$-equivariant bijection\n\n$$\\mathcal M^{\\mathrm{ADHM,reg}}_{k,N}\\;\\longleftrightarrow\\;\\mathcal M^{\\mathrm{ASD}}_{k,N}.$$\n\nThe zero-FI real quotient is also diffeomorphic to the stable-and-costable complex $GL(k)$ quotient. Under the stated projective GAGA and family base-change hypotheses, the corresponding framed sheaves on $\\mathbb P^2$ are exactly the locally free locus among the framed torsion-free sheaves with rank $N$ and Hilbert polynomial $N\\binom{m+2}{2}-k$. The positive-FI stable quotient includes non-locally-free sheaves and is not identified with the ordinary framed ASD moduli. Under the same family and normal-form hypotheses, the correspondence is compatible with first-order framed deformations and their tangent spaces.",
