          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $E\\to S^4$ be a smooth Hermitian rank-$N$ vector bundle with $N\\geq2$, a smooth unitary connection $A$, and a unitary framing at $\\infty$. Give $S^4$ the round metric and the orientation specified in the definition of the framed ASD sector, and assume $F_A^+=0$. Then the induced determinant-line connection on $\\det E=\\Lambda^N E$ is flat. Its framing at $\\infty$ determines a unique global unit parallel section, so the framed unitary bundle reduces to a framed $SU(N)$ bundle. With $q_N=-(8\\pi^2)^{-1}\\int_{S^4}\\operatorname{tr}_N(F_A\\wedge F_A)$ and the determinant Chern-form convention $c(A)=\\det(I-F_A/(2\\pi i))$, one has\n\n$$q_N(E,A)=-\\langle c_2(E),[S^4]\\rangle\\in-\\mathbb Z_{\\geq0}.$$\n\nThus $k=-q_N=\\langle c_2(E),[S^4]\\rangle$ is a nonnegative integer, with the sign corresponding to the anti-self-dual equation $F_A^+=0$.",
